      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I encountered the issue before and I investigated it for writing new canny, but I found this canny so I'm submitting additional information as comment here. (splitted to three due to limits)\n\n**Consistent Steps to Reproduce**\n\nWith these steps below, users can consistently reproduce the issue.\n\nIn real-world cases, this issue can also be reproduced by the Unity Editor crash during the build process.\n\n1. Prepare some new avatar with no blueprintId set, and enter the new avatar information including thumbnail in the VRChat SDK control panel.\n\n2. Click \"Build & Upload\" button to initiate the upload process.\n\n3. When the VRChat SDK asks for \"Copyright ownership agreement\", click \"x\" to close and terminate the upload process.\n\n4. Re-assign the thumbnail image in the VRChat SDK control panel.\n\n5. The VRChat SDK shows \"Save Changes\" button at the top of the control panel. Click it to save the changes.\n\n6. Re-initiate the upload process by clicking \"Build & Upload\" button again.\n\n7. Click \"OK\" on the \"Copyright ownership agreement\" dialog to proceed with the upload.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "_id": "68fafe7f1fe08c9a842bd25b",
      "aiGenerated": false,
      "author": {
        "_id": "5e4ca2145f9b3726b3b389e7",
        "alias": "Wild strawberry Canidae",
        "aliasID": "65c26ed9ed6eefce4c854f57",
